description:
Edit repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts with a REPLACE operation on the existing file. Do not use create_file — the file exists at roughly 181000 bytes and create_file will be refused.

Make exactly one replacement.

old_string (three lines, occurs exactly once; six spaces before continue, four before the closing brace, four before actionableGaps):
      continue;
    }
    actionableGaps.push(g);

new_string (the same two remaining lines, byte-identical, continue line removed):
    }
    actionableGaps.push(g);

Nothing else changes. Do not comment the line out — a prior attempt did and the semantic gate correctly hard-failed it as "zero behaviour delta". Do not anchor on a bare `continue;`, which occurs twice in this file. Do not rely on line numbers; this file shifts as other changes land.

Why: that `continue` sits in the `if (hopeless(g))` branch of pickMostLandable and drops every gap in a hopeless category before scoring runs. 23 documentation_drift gaps already compute to landability 1.00, joint top of the pool, and are never selected because of it. Removing it lets them reach actionableGaps and be scored — the "re-test path (penalty, not hard exclusion)" the comment above hopeless() already promises. Keep the uiQuestion_write escalation exactly as it is. Do not alter hopeless(), landabilityScore, or any threshold, and introduce no new symbol.

